  "details": "If I try to upload a part of the world, I will not be able to upload it because the Blueprint ID is not accessible on the screen where the configuration screen after the build should be displayed.\nI tried to detach the blueprint ID, change to another ID, re-open Unity, and pre-login to the API server, but there was no improvement.\nGiven the following error during upload, the large world that takes more than 5 minutes to build, and the recent prevalence of DDoS, I suspect that DDoS Protection's automatic logout is preventing us from seeing the blueprint ID.\n\nI am trying to upload the world from Japan.\n\n[<color=orange>Always</color>] Could not authenticate - Not logged in\nUnityEngine.Debug:LogError(Object, Object)\nVRC.Core.Logger:LogError(String, DebugLevel, Object)\nVRCSDK2.<>cDisplayClass35_0:<Start>b0(String) (at Assets/VRCSDK/Dependencies/VRChat/Scripts/RuntimeWorldCreation.cs:96)\nVRCSDK2.RuntimeWorldCreation:Start() (at Assets/VRCSDK/Dependencies/VRChat/Scripts/RuntimeWorldCreation.cs:102)",
